// Result discipline, enforced.
//
// CLAUDE.md invariant: "Every mutation returns Result<T, MutationError>. Don't
// throw across mutation boundaries." The mutation and theme layers hold to that
// today — this keeps it true. A thrown error skips the typed union entirely, so
// the HTTP status table, the MCP error envelope and the canvas's renderer all
// lose their guarantee at once.
//
// Scoped by `overrides` in biome.json to the layers that owe a Result; every
// other package still throws freely. Lifting a throwing API into a Result is
// what `tryCatchAsync` is for.
language js

`throw $error` where {
  register_diagnostic(span=$error, message="This layer returns Result<T, E> — return `err(...)` instead of throwing. Wrap a throwing dependency with tryCatchAsync at the boundary.")
}
